anding force vectors is crucial for analyzing joint stress, muscle function during exercises, and optimizing technique to apply force effectively (e.g., aligning muscle force with desired movement direction).\n\n\\*\\*Key Research:\\*\\*  \n\\- Nordin M, Frankel VH. (2012). Basic Biomechanics of the Musculoskeletal System (4th ed.). Lippincott Williams & Wilkins.  \n\\- Enoka RM. (2015). Neuromechanics of Human Movement (5th ed.). Human Kinetics.\n\n\\*\\*Links:\\*\\* [[A11. Biomechanics Levers in the Human Body]], [[A13. Biomechanics Torque and Movement]], [[A18. Proper Lifting Mechanics]]'}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514'}}
