2025-06-05 00:59:22,194 - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/v1/messages', 'timeout': Timeout(connect=5.0, read=600, write=600, pool=600), 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-9dbe006e-6780-47a4-9d5d-017806135a63', 'json_data': {'max_tokens': 4000, 'messages': [{'role': 'user', 'content': 'You are rewriting fitness/exercise science notes for better accessibility while maintaining scientific rigor. This is part of an interconnected Obsidian knowledge base.\n\nCRITICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n1. NEVER change the note title - this breaks links across the entire library\n2. PRESERVE all existing [[links]] exactly as written - do not modify anything inside [[ ]]\n3. MAINTAIN all scientific accuracy and citations\n4. ADD practical applications if missing\n5. ENSURE all key claims are backed by research citations\n6. Use the exact structure provided below\n\nSTANDARD NOTE STRUCTURE:\n```markdown\n### [Original Title - NEVER CHANGE]\n**ID:** [Keep original ID exactly as is]\n**Created:** [Original date] (Updated: [Current date])\n\n## Quick Takeaway\n[Single sentence bottom line - what users need to know immediately]\n\n## Key Points\n- [3-5 factual bullet points explaining core concepts]\n- [No performance percentages or claims like "increases by X%"]\n- [Focus on what happens, not how much improvement]\n- [Example: "Type I fibers are fatigue resistant and recruited first" not "Type I training improves endurance by 20%"]\n\n## Deep Dive\n[Your original detailed content - reorganized with subheadings]\n[Preserve ALL scientific accuracy and mechanisms]\n[Use clear subheadings for complex topics]\n[Include inline citations for key claims]\n\n### [Subheading as needed]\n[Detailed explanations with citations]\n\n## Research Evidence\n[MANDATORY: ALL citations must have working DOI or PMID links]\n[Format: Author et al. (Year). Title. Journal, Volume(Issue), Pages. DOI: https://doi.org/[DOI]]\n[If no DOI: Author et al. (Year). Title. Journal, Volume(Issue), Pages. PMID: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/[PMID]]\n[Highlight key findings and effect quality]\n[Remove any citations without verifiable links]\n\n## Practical Applications\n[How to actually implement this - ADD if missing]\n[Specific examples, numbers, protocols]\n[Real-world scenarios]\n\n## Common Mistakes\n⚠️ [What people typically get wrong]\n⚠️ [Misconceptions to avoid]\n⚠️ [Implementation errors]\n\n## Related Concepts\n[PRESERVE ALL EXISTING LINKS EXACTLY]\n[Add contextual phrases around links where helpful]\n[Example: "adequate protein intake [[B2. Protein Requirements]]" instead of just "[[B2. Protein Requirements]]"]\n\n## Update Log\n- [Date]: [What changed and why]\n```\n\nLINKING PRESERVATION RULES:\n- Keep all [[Note Name]] links exactly as they appear\n- You can add descriptive text around links: "adequate protein intake [[B2. Protein Requirements]]"\n- Never modify what\'s inside the [[ ]] brackets\n- Never change link destinations\n\nRESEARCH CITATION RULES:\n- Preserve all existing citations\n- Add inline citations for key claims\n- MANDATORY: Include valid DOI links for ALL research citations\n- Format: Author et al. (Year). Title. Journal, Volume(Issue), Pages. DOI: https://doi.org/[DOI]\n- If no DOI available, include PubMed PMID: https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/[PMID]\n- Ensure all major claims are backed by research with working links\n- Do NOT include citations without verifiable links\n- Remove any citations that cannot be verified with DOI or PMID\n\nHere\'s the note to rewrite:\n\n# A62. Metabolic Flexibility Training\n\n**ID:** A62-METABOLIC-FLEXIBILITY-TRAINING\n**Created:** 2025-04-26 (Updated: 2025-01-14)\n\n## Quick Takeaway\n\nMetabolic flexibility training involves optimizing the body\'s ability to switch between different fuel sources efficiently, including assessment of substrate utilization, energy metabolism, and performance optimization.\n\n## Key Points\n\n- Substrate switching improves by 20-30% with targeted training\n- Energy efficiency increases by 15-25% with proper protocols\n- Performance optimization enhances by 25-35% with optimal training\n- Recovery outcomes improve by 20-40% with systematic practice\n- Endurance capacity increases by 25-35% with appropriate management\n\n## Deep Dive\n\n### Training Components\n\n**Metabolic Analysis:**\n\n1. **Substrate Utilization**\n\n   - Carbohydrate metabolism\n   - Fat oxidation\n   - Energy efficiency\n   - Performance factors\n   - Risk assessment\n\n2. **Response Assessment**\n   - Metabolic analysis\n   - Energy evaluation\n   - Performance optimization\n   - Risk management\n   - Adaptation patterns\n\n**Performance Components:**\n\n1. **Utilization Patterns**\n\n   - Substrate patterns\n   - Energy patterns\n   - Performance patterns\n   - Recovery patterns\n   - Risk patterns\n\n2. **Flexibility Management**\n   - Utilization optimization\n   - Energy enhancement\n   - Performance improvement\n   - Risk reduction\n   - Adaptation management\n\n## Research Evidence\n\nGoodpaster, B.H., & Sparks, L.M. (2017). Metabolic flexibility in health and disease. Cell Metabolism. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cmet.2017.05.013\n\nGalgani, J.E., & Ravussin, E. (2008). Energy metabolism, fuel selection and body weight regulation. International Journal of Obesity. https://doi.org/10.1038/ijo.2008.246\n\nHolloszy, J.O. (2005). Exercise-induced increase in muscle insulin sensitivity. Journal of Applied Physiology. https://doi.org/10.1152/japplphysiol.00123.2005\n\n## Practical Applications\n\n**Assessment Protocols:**\n\n1. **Utilization Assessment**\n\n   - Metabolic analysis\n   - Energy evaluation\n   - Performance assessment\n   - Risk identification\n   - Adaptation patterns\n\n2. **Performance Development**\n   - Utilization optimization\n   - Energy enhancement\n   - Performance improvement\n   - Risk reduction\n   - Adaptation management\n\n**Implementation Guidelines:**\n\n1. **Technical Assessment**\n\n   - Metabolic analysis\n   - Energy evaluation\n   - Performance metrics\n   - Technical emphasis\n   - Optimization focus\n\n2. **Performance Analysis**\n   - Utilization optimization\n   - Performance assessment\n   - Risk evaluation\n   - Technical emphasis\n   - Optimization focus\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n⚠️ **Assessment without proper context** - Systematic evaluation is essential\n\n⚠️ **Ignoring utilization patterns** - Each pattern requires specific attention\n\n⚠️ **Poor assessment methods** - Analysis must match flexibility requirements\n\n⚠️ **Inadequate metrics** - Proper measurement is crucial for optimization\n\n## Related Concepts\n\nMetabolic flexibility training directly informs [[A63. pH Regulation Mechanisms]] and [[A64. Oxygen Sensing Pathways]]. It\'s crucial for [[X12. Vertical Jump Training]] and [[X11. Sprinting]]. Modern assessment tools are discussed in [[VIII-3. Wearable Technology (Fitness Trackers, Smartwatches, HRMs)]].\n\n## Update Log\n\n- 2025-01-14: Created with practical applications and common mistakes section, maintained scientific accuracy and citations\n'}], 'model': 'claude-sonnet-4-20250514', 'system': 'You are a fitness science expert helping to improve the accessibility and clarity of exercise science notes while maintaining scientific accuracy.', 'temperature': 0.7}}
